id: pm-gh1383
title: "GH-1383: consistent SDK item/history drift reads during concurrent ordinary mutations"
description: "History drift validation can compare different item/history versions while a legitimate writer advances one item, reporting transient corruption although quiescent validation is clean. Preserve strict stable-corruption detection while observing a consistent read or bounded per-item retry."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: context-management,github-intake,read-consistency
created_at: "2026-10-03T22:14:16.447Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-04T08:10:18.333Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-04T08:10:17.655Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-04T08:10:17.655Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Real isolated overlapping validation and comment append reproduces the old failure;Consistent-read or bounded retry eliminates false item mismatch;Genuine stable corruption remains a strict failure;Source and cache scans retain complete omission and integrity receipts
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Consistent SDK item/history reads now recheck item-hash discrepancies under ordinary writer locks, preserve independent corruption/identity/repair diagnostics and preserve the full-corpus cache."
expected_result: "Ordinary concurrent writers must not cause stale-snapshot corruption findings; actual corruption, contention and missing canonical sources must remain explicit failures."
actual_result: "Real isolated regressions and Node/Bun 152-item overlapping reads/writes retain zero hash/chain discrepancies; stable tampering, independent identities, missing source and lock contention remain failures. Complete source suite: 9686 passed, 2 Windows-only Linux skips and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage."
