comments[14]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-03T22:14:16.447Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: fresh strict all-status full-body corpus 2868/2868 complete with zero unreadable records and zero omissions. Exact GH1383 and concurrent history-validation predicates have no canonical leaf. Closed pm-eax4y8 full metadata/comments and verified full history establish a different authoritative-projection/cache cause. Current open and in_progress inventories were read; this new report stays open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-04T03:34:10.681Z","harness:codex","Investigation and TDD plan: source item documents are loaded before sequential history verification, so an ordinary writer can advance the stream after the document snapshot. Recheck only discrepant pairs against authoritative storage while holding the existing per-item writer lock; preserve strict corruption verdicts and bound contention. Retain core snapshot semantics for caller-provided documents and do not use history compaction. Regression owners are real SDK persistence and subprocess CLI transport, without test-only exports."
  "2026-10-04T03:51:21.791Z","harness:codex","TDD: 137 focused tests pass, including real annotation CLI transports, declared help recovery, stable history corruption, cache preservation and lock contention. All three isolated safe controls pass; restoring each unsafe invariant fails its selected behavior assertion. No source coverage exclusions or threshold changes. Full-source coverage and static release gates are now running before closure."
  "2026-10-04T03:57:53.725Z","harness:codex","Manual acceptance on isolated Node and Bun workspaces uses real CLI annotation transports, claim/close/release and public SDK ordinary-writer overlap over 152 items. Node acceptance has passed; Bun is still executing. Packed npm/npx/bunx acceptance independently passed with nine bundled packages. Live Sentry/required telemetry gate passes with zero recent unresolved Sentry issues, telemetry error rate 1.44 percent and zero missing error-code rows. These observations are distinct from a future release of this branch."
  "2026-10-04T04:03:20.015Z","harness:codex","Linked-test configuration correction: the none PM-context mode correctly refused source-workspace execution before invoking the command. Retained that immutable refusal evidence and replaced the link through the CLI with schema isolation. The regression controller itself copies source into a disposable workspace and runs the canonical isolated test runner. No trust, isolation or failure gate was relaxed."
  "2026-10-04T04:10:36.882Z","harness:codex","Current live repository verification passes history drift and storage integrity with zero missing/unreadable streams, hash/chain mismatches, version skew or singleton-state mismatches. Resolution diagnostics retain 170 historical missing-field warnings; these are not rewritten as newly proven outcomes. The published 2026.10.4 Auto Release and all npm/Bun acceptance jobs are successful, latest npm is 2026.10.4, and the same-day guard refuses a second version. This branch remains unpublished until a later eligible release."
  "2026-10-04T04:25:56.264Z","harness:codex","Full-suite integration feedback: chain-only corruption has independent stream evidence and must preserve the existing merge-repair failure envelope even when a stale lock prevents repair. Restrict canonical locked rechecks to item-hash discrepancies; retain strict chain-only findings directly. Missing canonical source for an item-hash discrepancy now returns item_not_found rather than certifying a stale pair. Added multiple independent identity-corruption and runtime-declared command cases. The local npm fixture requires correct discovery of the actual globally installed npm package; use an ephemeral NODE_PATH for this host instead of modifying product behavior or weakening checks."
  "2026-10-04T04:36:40.160Z","harness:codex","Full-suite feedback: restrict consistent rereads to item-hash discrepancies. History-only corruption continues to reach repair diagnostics without acquiring a second item lock. Existing lock-owner repair regression passes. Generated error catalog now records the governance owner of item_not_found. No coverage denominator or threshold changes."
  "2026-10-04T04:39:21.125Z","harness:codex","Verification environment finding: the packed continuation regression passes unchanged when npm packing runs after the build completes and with one test worker. Its real tarball consumer verified all 11 list/search/context scenarios. Four earlier 30-second suite timeouts also pass with one worker (39/39 assertions). Local verification will serialize build, package inspection and canonical coverage to avoid competing file-generation work; test budgets and source coverage gates remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-04T06:34:44.625Z","harness:codex","Generated contracts snapshot was refreshed with the owning generator after the mandatory stale-snapshot gate refused it. The complete diff adds only sdk/governance/validate-history-drift.ts to the existing item_not_found source catalog; no error identity, flag, or public command shape changes. The generated fixture is linked to this history-validation owner. Complete typecheck passed all four configurations; whole static verification continues with unchanged gates."
  "2026-10-04T06:47:43.248Z","harness:codex","Assurance attribution is explicit: the disposable controller is exercised by its real unit owner in mandatory full-source coverage. Structured gate_evidence therefore names the registered test-coverage gate strengthened by the regressions, rather than implying a separate standalone assurance gate for the controller. The registered recurrence population now passes172/172 members across58 lineages and117 edges, with24 families and zero missing or uncovered members. No association/hierarchy edge is treated as recurrence proof."
  "2026-10-04T06:57:36.311Z","harness:codex","Complete current-source static prefix passes dependency audit and embedded bundles, docstring ratchet, dead exports, ESLint, three zero-duplicate gates, permissions/cooldown, generation/contracts, package/surface/grammar/refusal/token/MCP gates, all47 tracker-context assertions, gate registry and unchanged public SDK surface (zero classified changes), plus10 SDK entrypoint import budgets. Node26.9 CLI admission fails get366>362ms, next447>440ms, create414>398ms on unchanged ceilings. The receipt remains failed. Complete pipeline is being verified under installed CI-admission Node24.12.0 without host configuration changes or budget adjustments; no cause or patch-specific attribution is claimed from the Node26 failure."
  "2026-10-04T07:45:15.445Z","harness:codex","Shared linked acceptance 2026-10-04: pm test-all selected four active items and seven links, ran four unique commands successfully, and explicitly skipped three duplicate controller links. The shared controller baseline proved all four real source conditions, and the source coverage suite independently runs all four unsafe-source assertion controls. Complete component-by-component static, manual Node/Bun, packaged-consumer and reliability receipts are recorded on the shared verification owner. Final exact all-source coverage remains pending and is not claimed complete by this comment."
  "2026-10-04T08:10:16.842Z","harness:codex","TDD: final all-source coverage passed unchanged exact gates: 9686 tests passed, 2 Windows-only skips on Linux; lines=63515/63515, statements=66625/66625, functions=13761/13761, branches=50965/50965. Zero uncovered counts across every measured source file. Focused real regressions, unsafe-source controls, linked execution and temporary Node/Bun/npm/npx/bunx acceptance passed. Implementation, closure and package-owned changelog are carried on the same delivery branch; published 2026.10.4 predates this change."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-04T04:08:57.073Z","harness:codex","SDK validation boundary: preserve the core supplied-snapshot API and its strict corruption semantics. The higher-level validator rechecks only discrepant canonical items under ordinary mutation locks, honoring custom schemas and type folders. Selective verification disables cache writes so full-corpus entries are retained; workspace singleton diagnostics are preserved. Lock conflicts and unreadable source propagate without force or certainty claims."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-04T05:30:29.209Z","harness:codex","Retained repair-lock integration tests caught a lock interaction that the focused race tests did not cover. Consistent reads and repair diagnostics have distinct ownership: recheck source-hash discrepancies under a writer lock, while keeping history-only findings available without acquiring another lock. Real source mutation controls prove the targeted regression; they complement the unchanged whole-suite contracts."
